# Greensleeves, arranged for the Orchestral style.
# Flute and harp first, then violins and strings; the flute returns an octave up.
title: Greensleeves
composer: Traditional (English)
arranger: Claude & SZ
about: An English ballad from the 1500s. Legend says Henry VIII wrote it for Anne Boleyn, but its style points to a later, unknown composer. The same tune carries the carol What Child Is This?
year: traditional
source: public-domain
category: classics
style: orchestral
key: A minor
tempo: 90
time: 3/4

